Chapter: SpikeMain
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Sky
  cites Poc chapter Spike
  cites Poc chapter SpikePrint

 SPIKE ONLY. THROWAWAY. Prints the speed profile and two still frames' draw
 commands as text, for harness/spike_svg.py to turn into a picture and for
 harness/metal.py --entry to compare against bare metal.

 TWO VIEWPOINTS PER ENTRY, AND AS OF 2026-08-30 THAT IS HABIT RATHER THAN NEED.
 The prelude never reclaims (C6) and neither arm has an arena rewind, so one run
 holds every frame it prints -- and while the printers concatenated left to right
 they held a QUADRATIC amount of it, which is what actually set the ceiling. Six
 viewpoints used to exhaust a native 4 GiB reserve and five a guest's 3072 MB.
 With `SpikePrint`'s halving fix an entry peaks at 133 MB and all eight would fit
 in one binary (C17).

 The pairs are kept because they exist, are tested, and give the guest one entry
 at a time to fail in. They are no longer the difference between running and not.

 The eight viewpoints are four entries of two, each named for what it looks at:
 this one, `SpikePondMain`, `SpikeCatMain` and `SpikeTruckMain`, with the speed
 profile in a fifth, `SpikeProfileMain`. Each is a chapter
 rather than a cite of this one, because a bundle is ONE FLAT NAMESPACE and two
 `opening`s collide -- B5, found by trying it. The printing they share is
 `Poc chapter SpikePrint`, cited rather than repeated, so the four FRAME binaries
 emit one format and spike_svg.py reads every entry's output concatenated without
 knowing how many produced it. SpikeProfileMain does not cite SpikePrint: a profile
 point is not a draw command. harness/spike.sh names all five once and runs them.

 THE PROFILE MOVED OUT on 2026-08-30, when coordinates became bit patterns. It is
 ONE line, but building it is quadratic -- `prof-all` concatenates right-recursively,
 so a 4,000-point line allocates the sum of its own prefixes -- and at roughly forty
 characters a point that was 160 MB while at eighty it is 640 MB. Beside two frames
 that exhausted the 4 GiB reserve outright. `Poc chapter SpikeProfileMain` has it,
 and the happy consequence is that every entry here is now exactly two viewpoints.

 We say:

Section: Entry

 One block per viewpoint.

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (scene-line "pig-herd" u-pig-herd)
    print-line-uni (all-cmds (spike-frame-at u-pig-herd) 0)
    print-line-uni (scene-line "mid-tower" u-mid-tower)
    print-line-uni (all-cmds (spike-frame-at u-mid-tower) 0)
  end
